#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:229 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:239
msgid "Use after scope"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:231
msgid ""
"This check warns when a pointer or reference is used after the stack "
"variable it refers to has gone out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:240 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:276
#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:307 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:344
#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:397
msgid "Correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:265 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:275
msgid "Use after free"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:267
msgid ""
"This check warns when a pointer or reference is used after the object it "
"refers to has been freed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:295 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:306
msgid "Return of stack address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:297
msgid ""
"This check warns when a function returns a pointer or reference to a stack-"
"allocated variable, which will be destroyed when the function returns, "
"leaving the caller with a dangling pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:333 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:343
msgid "Dangling field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:335
msgid ""
"This check warns when a constructor or method assigns a pointer to a stack-"
"allocated variable or temporary to a field of the class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:378 ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:396
msgid "Use after invalidation (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:380
msgid ""
"This check warns when a pointer, reference or view is used after an "
"operation that may have invalidated it. This includes references to "
"container elements used after a container operation, and pointers to objects "
"managed by owners such as `std::unique_ptr` after operations like `reset`. "
"For example, adding elements to `std::vector` may cause reallocation, "
"invalidating all existing iterators, pointers and references to its elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:388
msgid ""
"Invalidation checking is highly experimental and may produce false positives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:420
msgid ""
"The analysis also treats explicit destruction as invalidation. Explicit "
"destructor calls and `std::destroy_at` invalidate pointers, references and "
"views into the destroyed object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:443
msgid "Annotation Inference and Suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:445
msgid ""
"In addition to detecting lifetime violations, the analysis can suggest "
"adding `[[clang::lifetimebound]]` to function parameters or methods when it "
"detects that a pointer/reference to a parameter or `this` escapes via the "
"return value. This helps improve API contracts and allows the analysis to "
"perform more accurate checks in calling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:451
msgid "To enable annotation suggestions, use `-Wlifetime-safety-suggestions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:453
msgid ""
"Fix-it hints normally insert `[[clang::lifetimebound]]`. If a visible object-"
"like macro expands to `[[clang::lifetimebound]]` or "
"`__attribute__((lifetimebound))`, Clang will use the last such macro visible "
"at the insertion point. To force a project-specific macro spelling, use `-"
"lifetime-safety-lifetimebound-macro=<macro>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:470
msgid "Translation-Unit-Wide Analysis and Inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:472
msgid ""
"By default, lifetime analysis is intra-procedural for error checking. "
"However, for annotation inference to be effective, lifetime information "
"needs to propagate across function calls. You can enable experimental "
"translation-unit-wide analysis using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:477
msgid ""
"`-flifetime-safety-inference`: Enables inference of `lifetimebound` "
"attributes across functions in a TU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:479
msgid ""
"`-fexperimental-lifetime-safety-tu-analysis`: Enables TU-wide analysis for "
"better inference results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:485
msgid "Warning flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:487
msgid ""
"Lifetime safety warnings are organized into hierarchical groups, allowing "
"users to enable categories of checks incrementally. For example, `-Wlifetime-"
"safety` enables all dangling pointer checks, while `-Wlifetime-safety-"
"permissive` enables only the high-confidence subset of these checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:492
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-all`: Enables all lifetime safety warnings, including "
"dangling pointer checks, annotation suggestions, and annotation validations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:493
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety`: Enables dangling pointer checks from both the "
"`permissive` and `strict` groups listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:495
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-permissive`: Enables high-confidence checks for dangling "
"pointers. **Recommended for initial adoption.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:497
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-use-after-scope`: Warns when a pointer to a stack "
"variable is used after the variable's lifetime has ended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:498
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-use-after-free`: Warns when a pointer to an object is "
"used after it's been freed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:499
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-return-stack-addr`: Warns when a function returns a "
"pointer or reference to one of its local stack variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:500
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-dangling-field`: Warns when a class field is assigned a "
"pointer to a temporary or stack variable whose lifetime is shorter than the "
"class instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:502
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-strict`: Enables stricter and experimental checks. These "
"may produce false positives in code that uses move semantics heavily, as the "
"analysis might conservatively assume a use-after-free even if ownership was "
"transferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:504
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-use-after-scope-moved`: Same as `-Wlifetime-safety-use-"
"after-scope` but for cases where the variable may have been moved from "
"before its destruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:505
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-return-stack-addr-moved`: Same as `-Wlifetime-safety-"
"return-stack-addr` but for cases where the variable may have been moved from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:506
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-dangling-field-moved`: Same as `-Wlifetime-safety-"
"dangling-field` but for cases where the variable may have been moved from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:507
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-invalidation`: Warns when a pointer, reference, iterator "
"or view is used after an operation that may invalidate it, such as container "
"mutation or explicit destruction (e.g., `std::unique_ptr::reset`, `std::"
"destroy_at`) (Experimental)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:509
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-suggestions`: Enables suggestions to add `[[clang::"
"lifetimebound]]` to function parameters and `this` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:511
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-intra-tu-suggestions`: Suggestions for functions local to "
"the translation unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:512
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-intra-tu-constructor-suggestions`: Suggestions for "
"constructors local to the translation unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:513
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-cross-tu-suggestions`: Suggestions for functions visible "
"across translation units (e.g., in headers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:514
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-cross-tu-constructor-suggestions`: Suggestions for "
"constructors visible across translation units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:516
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-validations`: Enables checks that validate existing "
"lifetime annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:518
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-noescape`: Warns when a parameter marked with `[[clang::"
"noescape]]` escapes the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:519
msgid ""
"`-Wlifetime-safety-lifetimebound-violation`: Warns when the analysis cannot "
"verify that the return value can be lifetime bound to a parameter marked "
"with `[[clang::lifetimebound]]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:521
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:523
msgid "Move Semantics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:525
msgid ""
"The analysis does not currently track ownership transfers through move "
"operations. Instead, it uses scope-based lifetime tracking: when an owner "
"goes out of scope, the analysis assumes the resource is destroyed, even if "
"ownership was transferred via `std::move()` or `std::unique_ptr::release()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:530
msgid ""
"This means that if a pointer or view is created from an owner, and that "
"owner is later moved-from and goes out of scope, the analysis will issue a `-"
"Wlifetime-safety-*-moved` warning. This warning indicates that the pointer "
"may be dangling, even though the resource may still be alive under a new "
"owner. These are often false positives when ownership has been safely "
"transferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:536
msgid ""
"To avoid these warnings and ensure correctness, follow the **\"move-first-"
"then-alias\"** pattern: create views or raw pointers *after* the ownership "
"transfer, sourcing them from the new owner rather than the original owner "
"that will go out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:541
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:549
msgid "Anti-Pattern: Aliasing Before Move"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:550
msgid "Good Practice: Move-First-Then-Alias"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:587
msgid ""
"The same principle applies when moving ownership using `std::unique_ptr::"
"release()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:610
msgid "`std::unique_ptr` with custom deleters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:612
msgid ""
"The analysis assumes standard ownership semantics for owner types like `std::"
"unique_ptr`: when a `unique_ptr` goes out of scope, it is assumed that the "
"owned object is destroyed and its memory is deallocated. However, `std::"
"unique_ptr` can be used with a custom deleter that modifies this behavior. "
"For example, a custom deleter might keep the memory alive by transferring it "
"to a memory pool, or simply do nothing, allowing another system to manage "
"the lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:620
msgid ""
"Because the analysis relies on scope-based lifetime for owners, it does not "
"support custom deleters that extend the lifetime of the owned object beyond "
"the lifetime of the `std::unique_ptr`. In such cases, the analysis will "
"assume the object is destroyed when the `std::unique_ptr` goes out of scope, "
"leading to false positive warnings if pointers to the object are used "
"afterward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:649
msgid "Dangling Fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:651
msgid ""
"The lifetime analysis is intra-procedural. It analyzes one function or "
"method at a time. This means if a field is assigned a pointer to a local "
"variable or temporary inside a constructor or method, and that local's "
"lifetime ends before the method returns, the analysis will issue a `-"
"Wlifetime-safety-dangling-field` warning. It must do so even if no *other* "
"method of the class ever accesses this field, because it cannot see how "
"other methods are implemented or used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:670
msgid ""
"In this case, `name_` dangles after the constructor finishes. Even if "
"`data()` is never called, the analysis flags the dangling assignment in the "
"constructor because it represents a latent bug. The recommended approach is "
"to ensure fields only point to objects that outlive the field itself, for "
"example by storing an owned object (e.g., `std::string`) or ensuring the "
"borrowed object (e.g., one passed by `const&`) has a sufficient lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:678
msgid "Performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../LifetimeSafety.md:680
msgid ""
"Lifetime analysis relies on Clang's CFG (Control Flow Graph). For functions "
"with very large or complex CFGs, analysis time can sometimes be significant. "
"To mitigate this, the analysis allows to skip functions where the number of "
"CFG blocks exceeds a certain threshold, controlled by the `-lifetime-safety-"
"max-cfg-blocks=N` language option."
msgstr ""
